Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.37,0:00:05.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Fourth track: data assimilation,\Nmerging a model with a few measurements.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.95,0:00:11.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Learned priors came in through compressed\Nlatent spaces, then diffusion models.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.49,0:00:16.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}And a library now plugs deep networks into\NKalman filters and variational methods.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.62,0:00:21.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}We found no diffusion prior used\Nthis way for conducting fluids.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.95,0:00:24.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Near a flip, the answer\Nhas two polarities,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.63,0:00:28.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}and a prior that ignores the\Nmirror could bias it toward one.
